# Rebrand allowlist (Requirement 11.3)
#
# Files/globs listed here are EXEMPT from the rebrand grep check in
# scripts/rebrand-check.mjs. A file is allowed to retain a legacy identifier
# (gitroom / gitroomhq / postiz) only for legal, historical, or
# documentation/migration reasons.
#
# Syntax: one glob per line. Lines starting with '#' are comments.
# Globs are matched against repo-relative POSIX paths.

# Legal / attribution — must preserve upstream notices (Requirement 10.1)
LICENSE
ATTRIBUTION.md
CHANGELOG.md
**/CHANGELOG.md

# Docs that reference the upstream project (Postiz) by name for attribution /
# fork context. These are intentional and must keep the credit.
README.md
CLAUDE.md

# Migration guide intentionally documents legacy env var names and the rebrand
# check itself, so it references the legacy names by design (Requirement 22.1).
docs/MIGRATION.md

# The check tooling itself and its allowlist contain the patterns as literals.
.rebrand-allowlist
scripts/rebrand-check.mjs

# Lockfile may contain transitive upstream package metadata outside our control.
pnpm-lock.yaml
